A||||7||fieroX||bought my rims tonight, need tire size recomendation||||1||
Z||000000||fieroX||12-04-2001||01:56 AM||||I bought these rims from <A HREF="http://www.tires.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tires.com</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.discounttiredirect.com/product/wheels/enkrsf.large.jpg"> <BR>they are 17x7's and I plan to use 245/45/17's on the back but im unsure as to the best size for the front.  I want the widest I can go without them sticking out the sides.  Maybe a 225/40/17?  would 225/45/17 look to tall?  thanks.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||12-04-2001||02:05 AM||||I have 17x7 40mm offset on the front of my 88, and they were perfect with a 215/40/17.  The tires were the perfect width for the wheel, and the wheel to the fender, so everything is completely flush.  Now all I have to do is lower the front another couple inches  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>  <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/fiero/flushside.jpg">  <P>I think that 245/45 will be too big for a 17x7.  I have 245/45 on my 8" wheels in the rear, and they are flush just like the fronts.  With 1" narrower wheels, the tires will bulge out a lot.<P>My .02 bucks.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*edited typo*<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroX||12-04-2001||02:16 AM||||Rare87GT has the stock 15x7's on his car, with 245/60/15's and they are perfectly flush.  I think the 45 series will compensate for the 2 extra inches of wheel. <BR>And arent the offsets of suspension different between the 87's and 88's?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroX||12-04-2001||02:19 AM||||Ok I see what you are saying now.  Ill do some measuring and see how bad it will bulge.  I dont think too much.  I have 275/60/15's on my firebird and they dont bulge that much on 8" rims, and Ive got 235/60's on the front and they dont bulge at all with 7" rims.  Maybe a 235/40/17.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||12-04-2001||07:02 AM||||the width of the tread pattern should be close to matching the rim width. any wider and you run the risk of unseating the tire in hard cornering.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||12-04-2001||07:59 AM||||I wouldn't do bigger than 235-40-17 in a 7" rim. But if you like the tall fat tire look then you can run the risk Roger mentioned.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sootah||12-04-2001||10:06 AM||||Now, if I were to want to have 18" rims that poke out of the wheel well <I>eeeever</I> so slightly, (Like 3/4" on the back and ½" on the front) what tire size/offset would I need to go?<P>I just like the muscley look when the tires are all huge and fat. Like on the old GTO's n' shìt.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__tig_sig2.gif">          <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AOL IM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLAMMED87GT||12-04-2001||02:05 PM||||I'm running 205/40/17 Nitto450 Extreme's on my 17x7. That's about as low as it gets on 17s. It's a pretty stiff ride. (I have also lowered my car though.)<P>They aren't too bad as far as performance.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
